{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018BpUP4gqpyX822UGAHM3bz","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd048-hostid\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/hostid: Print Numeric Host Identifier\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  The hostid utility prints the numeric identifier of the current host as an 8-digit\n6\t  hexadecimal number. While rarely used in modern systems, it appears in legacy license\n7\t  managers and system fingerprinting scripts. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew\n8\t  GNU reference binary (ghostid, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on stdout and exit\n9\t  code, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n10\t\n11\tgoals:\n12\t  - G1: Print the 32-bit host identifier as an 8-digit lowercase hexadecimal number.\n13\t  - G2: Reject any extra operands with an error message and nonzero exit.\n14\t\n15\trequirements:\n16\t  R1:\n17\t    title: Default behavior\n18\t    items:\n19\t      - R1.1:\n20\t          text: When invoked with no arguments, must print the 32-bit host identifier as an 8-digit lowercase hexadecimal number followed by a newline and exit 0.\n21\t      - R1.2:\n22\t          text: The value must be derived from the gethostid(3) syscall or equivalent system call on the current platform.\n23\t\n24\t  R2:\n25\t    title: Error handling\n26\t    items:\n27\t      - R2.1:\n28\t          text: If any extra operand is provided (beyond --help and --version), must print an error message to stderr and exit 1.\n29\t      - R2.2:\n30\t          text: Must not accept any flags other than --help and --version. Unknown flags must produce an error message to stderr and exit 1.\n31\t\n32\t  R3:\n33\t    title: Differential testing\n34\t    items:\n35\t      - R3.1:\n36\t          text: Differential tests must compare stdout output and exit codes between the Go binary and the reference binary (ghostid) via pkg/testutils.\n37\t      - R3.2:\n38\t          text: \"Tests must cover: normal invocation (no arguments), extra operand error, and unknown flag error.\"\n39\t      - R3.3:\n40\t          text: All differential tests must set LC_ALL=C in the environment.\n41\t\n42\tnon_goals:\n43\t  - cmd/hostid does not set the host identifier.\n44\t  - cmd/hostid does not support any formatting options.\n45\t\n46\tacceptance_criteria:\n47\t  - id: AC1\n48\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/hostid prints the host identifier in 8-digit hex, matching ghostid.\"\n49\t    traces:\n50\t      - R1.1\n51\t      - R1.2\n52\t  - id: AC2\n53\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/hostid extraarg exits 1 with an error message to stderr, matching ghostid.\"\n54\t    traces:\n55\t      - R1.1\n56\t      - R2.1\n57\t      - R2.2\n58\t      - R3.1\n59\t      - R3.2\n60\t  - id: AC3\n61\t    criterion: \"Differential test against ghostid passes for normal invocation and error cases.\"\n62\t    traces:\n63\t      - R2.1\n64\t      - R2.2\n65\t      - R3.1\n66\t      - R3.2\n67\t      - R3.3\n68\t  - id: AC4\n69\t    criterion: \"cmd/hostid compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n70\t    traces:\n71\t      - R1.1\n72\t      - R1.2\n73\t      - R2.1\n74\t      - R2.2\n75\t      - R3.1\n76\t      - R3.2\n77\t      - R3.3\n78\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2ef5bbbd-ba57-4428-9989-3502009a89fe","uuid":"d0e33b5d-4ac8-479e-9c35-4cae41b02411","timestamp":"2026-05-14T16:57:31.336Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5186/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd048-hostid.yaml","content":"id: srd048-hostid\ntitle: \"cmd/hostid: Print Numeric Host Identifier\"\n\nproblem: |\n  The hostid utility prints the numeric identifier of the current host as an 8-digit\n  hexadecimal number. While rarely used in modern systems, it appears in legacy license\n  managers and system fingerprinting scripts. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew\n  GNU reference binary (ghostid, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on stdout and exit\n  code, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Print the 32-bit host identifier as an 8-digit lowercase hexadecimal number.\n  - G2: Reject any extra operands with an error message and nonzero exit.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Default behavior\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: When invoked with no arguments, must print the 32-bit host identifier as an 8-digit lowercase hexadecimal number followed by a newline and exit 0.\n      - R1.2:\n          text: The value must be derived from the gethostid(3) syscall or equivalent system call on the current platform.\n\n  R2:\n    title: Error handling\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: If any extra operand is provided (beyond --help and --version), must print an error message to stderr and exit 1.\n      - R2.2:\n          text: Must not accept any flags other than --help and --version. Unknown flags must produce an error message to stderr and exit 1.\n\n  R3:\n    title: Differential testing\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: Differential tests must compare stdout output and exit codes between the Go binary and the reference binary (ghostid) via pkg/testutils.\n      - R3.2:\n          text: \"Tests must cover: normal invocation (no arguments), extra operand error, and unknown flag error.\"\n      - R3.3:\n          text: All differential tests must set LC_ALL=C in the environment.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/hostid does not set the host identifier.\n  - cmd/hostid does not support any formatting options.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/hostid prints the host identifier in 8-digit hex, matching ghostid.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/hostid extraarg exits 1 with an error message to stderr, matching ghostid.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"Differential test against ghostid passes for normal invocation and error cases.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"cmd/hostid compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n","numLines":78,"startLine":1,"totalLines":78}}}
