{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is requesting implementation of task #5186: create `cmd/hostid/main.go` for the go-unix-utils project. This is a stitch task in an automated code generation pipeline. The hostid utility must print the 32-bit host identifier as an 8-digit zero-padded lowercase hexadecimal number followed by a newline. It must support `--help` and `--version` flags, reject unknown flags and extra operands with errors to stderr, and call `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at startup. The task covers srd048-hostid requirements R1.1-R1.2 (core behavior) and R2.1-R2.2 (error handling). No test file is in scope for this task.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Go reimplementations of GNU coreutils with differential testing against Homebrew reference binaries\n   - SIGPIPE handler pattern: all cmd/ utilities must call `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at main start\n   - gethostid(3) syscall to obtain the 32-bit host identifier\n   - Design decision D2: cmd/ packages must NOT import `golang.org/x/sys` directly — must use `pkg/sys` or Go stdlib `syscall` package\n   - Copyright header required on every Go file (SPDX MIT)\n   - Function size hard limit: 40 lines\n   - File size limit: 500 lines\n   - No git commands allowed — orchestrator manages git externally\n   - Write all files before building/testing (implementation strategy from go_style_constitution)\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd048-hostid.yaml` (READ)\n     - Full SRD for hostid utility\n     - R1.1: Print 32-bit host identifier as 8-digit lowercase hex + newline, exit 0\n     - R1.2: Value from gethostid(3) syscall or equivalent\n     - R2.1: Extra operands → error to stderr, exit 1\n     - R2.2: Only --help/--version 