t host identifier as 8-digit zero-padded lowercase hex + newline\n     - Use `syscall.Gethostid()` or equivalent (not golang.org/x/sys directly)\n   - Verify: `go build -o bin/hostid ./cmd/hostid/` succeeds\n   - Verify: `go vet ./cmd/hostid/` reports no issues\n   - Verify: `bin/hostid` prints correct output\n   - Verify: `bin/hostid --help` works (exits 0)\n   - Verify: `bin/hostid --version` works (exits 0)\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading the SRD file at `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd048-hostid.yaml` and was about to begin implementing `cmd/hostid/main.go`. No code has been written yet. The SRD confirmed the requirements:\n   - R1.1: 8-digit lowercase hex output of host identifier\n   - R1.2: Value from gethostid(3) syscall\n   - R2.1: Error on extra operands\n   - R2.2: Error on unknown flags, only --help/--version accepted\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Create `cmd/hostid/main.go` implementing all four task requirements (R1-R4). The implementation should:\n   - Start with SPDX copyright header\n   - Call `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` first in main\n   - Parse flags (only --help and --version)\n   - Reject extra operands with error message to stderr, exit 1\n   - Use `syscall.Gethostid()` to get the host ID value\n   - Print with `fmt.Printf(\"%08x\\n\", hostid)`\n   \n   Then run `go build -o bin/hostid ./cmd/hostid/` and `go vet ./cmd/hostid/` to verify, followed by testing `bin/hostid`, `bin/hostid --help`, and `bin/hostid --version`.\n\n   Direct quote from task: \"files: - path: cmd/hostid/main.go, action: create, note: hostid utility -- prints 32-bit host identifier as 8-digit hex\"\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5186/2ef5bbbd-ba57-4428-9989-3502009a89fe.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it